context_info = ()
for d in context:
    result = llm_query("You are a cricket data extractor. Read the document below and identify any specific match that meets ALL of the following 9 constraints. If a match is found, output concise structured info for each candidate as specified; otherwise, output 'No match in this document'.\n\nConstraints (must ALL be satisfied):\n1) For the winning team, the sum of runs scored by all batters EXCEPT their single highest run-scorer is between 75 and 80 inclusive.\n2) The highest scorer of the losing team scored between 35 and 45 inclusive.\n3) That losing team's top-scorer had 'control' (batting control percentage) between 60% and 63% inclusive.\n4) The losing team won the toss.\n5) Both teams completed their full quota of overs, and the absolute difference between their run rates (runs per over) is greater than 6.0.\n6) The highest scorer of the winning team hit more sixes than fours in that innings.\n7) The highest scorer of the winning team also took exactly 2 wickets in the match.\n8) On the final ball of the winning team's innings, a batter was dismissed.\n9) Across the entire match, more than 6 batters (combined across both teams) had single-digit scores (0–9 inclusive).\n\nClarifications:\n- For constraint 1, compute: (sum of runs by all batters on the winning side) minus (runs by the single highest run-scorer of that side), and check if it is in [75, 80].\n- Run rate is total runs divided by overs faced; both must have batted full overs (e.g., 20 overs in T20, 50 in ODI, etc.).\n- 'Control' is a metric often presented as a percentage in ball-by-ball analytics; it must be explicitly present in the document.\n\nIf a match is found, provide for each candidate match:\n- Match number/ID/label (as written in the document):\n- Tournament/series name:\n- Year:\n- Teams and result (winner/loser):\n- Toss (who won):\n- Overs and totals for both teams; computed run rates for both:\n- Winning team's top-scorer: name, runs, 4s and 6s, confirmation of more 6s than 4s (Yes/No), wickets taken by that player (must be exactly 2):\n- Sum of runs by the rest of the winning team's batters (excluding the top-scorer):\n- Last ball of the winning team's innings was a wicket (Yes/No), and brief evidence:\n- Losing team's top-scorer: name, runs, control percentage:\n- Count of single-digit scores across the whole match:\n- Evidence quotes (copy exact lines from the document proving each point):\n- Meets all constraints: Yes/No (if No, list the specific constraint numbers that fail or are unknown)\n\nOnly use information directly found in this document; do not guess. Be concise but include the exact evidence lines.\n\nBEGIN_DOCUMENT\n" + d + "\nEND_DOCUMENT")
    context_info = context_info + (result,)

combined = "\n\n----- DOCUMENT ANALYSIS RESULT -----\n\n".join(context_info)

final_answer = llm_query("We need to find exactly one cricket match that satisfies ALL 9 constraints. Below are analyses (one per document). Choose the single match that satisfies all constraints, with explicit evidence where possible.\n\nAnalyses:\n" + combined + "\n\nInstructions:\n- If you identify exactly one match meeting all constraints, output ONLY one line in this exact format:\nMatch number | Tournament | Year\n- If multiple matches qualify, choose the one with the strongest explicit evidence and still output exactly one line as above.\n- If no match satisfies all constraints, output exactly:\nNot found\n\nDo not add any extra text or explanation. Just the single required line.")

return_result(final_answer)